        // lines say the page is turned a quarter either way (`rt-vertical`) and OSD names one (90 or 270), else 0. Tesseract's orientation is how the page IS
        // turned (90: its text runs bottom to top, and read upright a turn of 270 later), so the turn that makes it upright is the rest of the circle.
        int osd = Evidence.orGet(oruns, run, Evidence.orfOsd());
